{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790965028,"nonce":"+YKvMyPwwlXzCKg6ESbnlxFGwt8=","message":"Landed on branch `worktree-agent-a9ffedc5230b1e31b`:\n\n- `d255559a` doc: allocations design — `doc/design/allocations.md`, A1..A11.\n- `fda00554` schema: the `allocation` type in `schema.yaml`, imported into\n  the tracker. `iteration` (relation → iteration, inverse `allocations`),\n  `work` (relation → epic, story, inverse `staffing`), `assignee`, `points`.\n- `66e01c1c` tui: the `matrix` kind in `view/kinds.go`, `tui/matrix.go`,\n  `tui/matrix_view.go`, `tui/matrix_test.go`, wired in `tui/tui.go`;\n  `git work view matrix --help` and `work.view.matrix` both come from the\n  table, and both were checked.\n\nCalls made beyond the brief, all recorded in the design document:\n\n- **No status, no rank, no priority, no area on `allocation`** (A2). An\n  allocation is a plan, not a piece of work; a status would file it into\n  every `status != \"done\"` listing in this repository and make `overview`\n  and `board` report planning rows as work in flight. Removal is `archive`.\n- **The presets ship no `allocation` type** (A3). They are Jira's and\n  Linear's native models, neither has one, and the matrix kind needs no\n  particular type: `points by work by iteration` over allocations and\n  `estimate by story by sprint` over plain tasks are the same call.\n- **The two relations take two inverse names**, `allocations` and\n  `staffing`: an inverse is unique within the type that holds it\n  (`schema/document.go`), so one name for both is refused.\n- **A relation axis is ordered by the target's title**, not by the query's\n  order (A5). The query returns allocations, not sprints, so `sort_by`\n  could only reach the allocation's own fields, which hold a hash.\n  `row_values` / `column_values` with explicit ids is the override.\n- **`value` is a feature, not a defaulted argument** (A4): its absence is a\n  different view — the cells count — not a different default.\n- **`group_by` is blocks of rows under one column header** (A8), not a\n  matrix per group: the columns are the same axis in every group, and two\n  matrices at different widths cannot be compared down the screen.\n- **The filter narrows the axes, not the issues** (A9), and leaves whole an\n  axis nothing matches. Hiding issues would change every sum while the\n  totals still read as totals.\n- **The totals row and column are cells like any other**: the cursor sits\n  on them and `Enter` opens the whole row, column or matrix, which falls\n  out of the drill-down rather than being built.\n- **`M-c`/`Y` copies the cell's `git work view list …` command**, because a\n  cell has no id and what identifies it is exactly that query.\n- A multi-valued axis double-counts, by construction (A5).\n\n`go test ./...`, `go vet ./...` and `gofmt` are clean. The jira derive\ngoldens moved, because `jira/derive_test.go` derives against this\nrepository's own `schema.yaml`; the new type shows there as\n`info allocation: local-only type: never exported`, which is A3 working.\n\nDeferred, in the document: the GUI half (`8b06191`, as for every kind),\nand editing in the matrix, which belongs to actions-injected-into-views.\n\nThe design document was approved by the orchestrating agent, in Luis's\nplace, because he had left for the day.","files":null}]}